{
  "$comment": "Golden fixtures of plan §4.3 (W3-T6), recorded from the verified pinned CLI in the test-support sandbox (mock with egress trap, leak tracker, outside-write check) on Windows (subst-drive test root) and Linux (node:22-bookworm container), by RecordingSession and normalizeRecords of @hudhud/test-support. Paths, uuids, pids, versions, timestamps, durations and costs normalized; the fake key redacted. One file per suite, platform and case: <suite>/<platform>[.<case>].jsonl[.gz]. The suite scripts live in tooling/test-support/src/fixtures/record (pnpm fixtures:record, W3-Z); Re-recorded by W4-T2 with the product's own launch (the adapter's buildArgv and buildChildEnv with the sandbox environment as the parent; recorderRevision b06d075). This directory holds data only: the recordings and, next to each, its expect file <suite>/<platform>[.<case>].expect.jsonl (W4-T2), which no manifest entry lists and the recorder never writes.",
  "format": "conformance.schema.json record lines {\"t\",\"dir\",\"v\"}; the first line (dir \"config\") is the launch: argv after the binary and the extra environment. A host write of two lines is split into two \"in\" records with the same t (interrupt-same-write). The expect blocks of each recording are in its expect file, one conformance.schema.json expect line per record line (the effects and events of the session machine for that line, written by the update mode of the conformance runner and reviewed; packages/claude-code/test/conformance, W4-T2). A re-recording must be followed by the update mode and a reviewed expect diff.",
